    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Cardinality of a Set With Set Elements",
    "problem": "If $A={1,{10,12},15,{22,26,28},{42,62}}$, then $|A|=$",
    "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n1,\\,{10,12},\\,15,\\,{22,26,28},\\,{42,62}\n$$\n\nNote that ${10,12},$ ${22,26,28},$ and ${42,62}$ each count as single elements of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ has $5$ elements, the cardinality is $|A|=5.$",
